{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_31_1699533068#11_3485353544","relevance":2,"reason":"The full American Family Physician document is dedicated to child-abuse risk factors and lists prematurity as a child-related risk factor, while also discussing an ecological interaction of parent, family, community, and child factors and the extreme stress of a new infant. However, it does not explicitly explain why prematurity itself increases risk.","learned":"Prematurity is recognized in a clinical child-abuse prevention article as a child-related risk factor within an ecological model in which child vulnerability interacts with parental stress, poor coping, and lack of support."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ preterm premature prematurity) (+ maltreatment abuse neglect) (+ \"parental stress\" \"parenting stress\" attachment bonding))","reason":"Search for research or clinical sources that explicitly connect preterm birth with maltreatment risk through parenting stress, impaired attachment, or bonding problems."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ preterm premature prematurity) (+ maltreatment abuse neglect) (+ \"parental stress\" \"parenting stress\" attachment bonding))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_02_640062589#0_1116001376","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q747","rank":3,"snippet":"Attachment\" , \"segment\": \"risk for impaired parent/infant/ child Attachment | Nursing Dx risk for impaired parent/infant/ child Attachment 4:44 PM Posted by Pak Mantri Taxonomy II: Role Relationships—Class 2 Family Relationships (00058) [Diagnostic Division: Social Interaction] Submitted 1994 Definition: Disruption of the interactive process between parent/SO and infant that fosters the development of a protective and nurturing reciprocal relationship Risk Factors Inability of parents to meet personal needs Anxiety associated with the parent role Substance <cover>abuse Premature infant; ill infant/child who is unable to effectively initiate parental contact due to altered behavioral organization Separation; physical barriers Lack of privacy [Parents who themselves experienced altered attachment] [</cover>Uncertainty of paternity; conception as a result of rape/sexual abuse] [Difficult pregnancy and/or birth (actual or perceived)] NOTE: A risk diagnosis is not evidenced by signs and symptoms, as the problem has not occurred and nursing interventions are directed at prevention. Desired Outcomes/Evaluation Criteria—Parent Will: • Identify and prioritize family strengths and needs.\" , \"start_char\": 0.000000 , \"title\": \"risk for impaired parent/infant/ child Attachment | Nursing Dx\" , \"","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_130494300#1_148142872","rank":1,"relevance":1},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_130494300#0_148138636","rank":2,"relevance":1}]}}
