{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_51_1065794891#7_2188158776","relevance":3,"reason":"This emergency medicine child-abuse curriculum is dedicated to child abuse/non-accidental trauma and directly explains the point: characteristics that make a child more difficult to care for predispose to maltreatment, and premature delivery may increase vulnerability to abuse.","learned":"Prematurity can be a risk factor because child characteristics that make care more difficult or increase vulnerability predispose to maltreatment; premature delivery is specifically named as increasing vulnerability to abuse."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ premature prematurity preterm \"low birth weight\") (+ \"abusive head trauma\" \"shaken baby syndrome\" \"child abuse\") (+ risk stress crying))","reason":"Look for additional direct evidence in abusive head trauma/shaken baby syndrome sources, where prematurity may be linked to caregiver stress, crying, and vulnerability."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ premature prematurity preterm \"low birth weight\") (+ \"abusive head trauma\" \"shaken baby syndrome\" \"child abuse\") (+ risk stress crying))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_930063563#12_2018964925","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q749","rank":1,"snippet":"What causes shaken baby syndrome? What are the risk factors for shaken baby syndrome? SLIDESHOW What are shaken baby syndrome symptoms and signs? Latest Healthy Kids News Daily Health News Trending on MedicineNet How do physicians diagnose shaken baby syndrome? What is the treatment for shaken baby syndrome? What are complications and long-term effects of shaken baby syndrome? Subscribe to MedicineNet's General Health Newsletter What is the prognosis of shaken baby syndrome? Is it possible to prevent <cover>shaken baby syndrome? What can caregivers or parents do to calm a crying baby? From Parenting & Children's Health Resources Health Solutions From Our Sponsors Health Solutions From Our Sponsors \" , \"segment\": \"High-risk infants (premature </cover>babies, those with chronic medical conditions, etc.) commonly extract an even higher toll on parents. This may be due to the more demanding requirements of such children and/or a belief of an increase in infant vulnerability. For some caregivers, physical punishment represents the only way to free themselves of their frustrations. What are the risk factors for shaken baby syndrome? Risk factors for shaken baby syndrome (as well as other types of inflicted trauma on children) may be conceptualized "}}
