{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_930063563#12_2018964925","relevance":3,"reason":"This shaken baby syndrome/inflicted trauma source directly answers the information need: premature babies are high-risk infants who place a higher toll on parents because they may have more demanding care requirements and perceived increased vulnerability; caregiver frustration can lead to physical punishment/abuse.","learned":"Prematurity increases child-abuse risk in part because premature infants often require more demanding care, are perceived as more vulnerable, and can increase caregiver stress and frustration, which are risk factors for inflicted trauma such as shaken baby syndrome."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q749","reason":"The abusive head trauma/shaken baby query produced a direct grade-3 result; continue to find more sources with the same mechanism."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q749"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_07_1278738455#4_2316897101","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q749","rank":3,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_07_1278738455#4_2316897101\" , \"end_char\": 4114.000000 , \"headings\": \"Colic Colic Overview Symptoms When to see a doctor Causes<cover>Risk factors Complications Shaken baby syndrome Request an Appointment at Mayo Clinic Colic \" , \"segment\": \"Sex of the child Preterm </cover>and full-term pregnancies Formula-fed and breast-fed babies Infants born to mothers who smoked during pregnancy or after delivery have an increased risk of developing colic. Complications Colic does not cause short-term or long-term medical problems for a child. Colic is stressful for parents. Research has shown an association between colic and the following problems with parent well-being: Increased risk of postpartum depression in mothers Early cessation of breast-feeding Feelings of guilt, exhaustion, helplessness or anger Shaken baby syndrome The stress of calming a crying baby has sometimes prompted parents to shake or otherwise harm their child. Shaking a baby can cause serious damage to the brain and death. The risk of these uncontrolled reactions is greater if parents don't have information about soothing a crying child, ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_49_126583413#2_254044156","rank":2,"relevance":1}]}}
{"request":{"judgments":"14/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_07_1278738455#4_2316897101","relevance":1,"reason":"This Mayo Clinic colic page explains that infant crying/colic can create parental stress, anger, helplessness, and sometimes shaken baby syndrome, but it does not identify prematurity as a reason for increased abuse risk; preterm/full-term is only mentioned under colic risk factors.","learned":"Excessive crying can stress caregivers and lead to shaking or harm, which is a relevant mechanism, but this result does not connect that mechanism specifically to prematurity."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"premature infants\" (+ \"risk of abuse\" \"at risk for abuse\" maltreatment) (+ demanding vulnerable stress))","reason":"Search for direct phrasing that premature infants are at risk for abuse with the explanatory mechanisms of demanding care, vulnerability, and caregiver stress."}}
