{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_31_680964661#27_1341245606","relevance":2,"reason":"This non-accidental trauma document directly lists premature or low birth weight infants, frequent crying, and special needs/disabilities as infant characteristics that make abuse more likely. However, the snippet does not explain why prematurity increases risk beyond association with vulnerable/high-need infant characteristics.","learned":"Premature or low-birth-weight infants are listed among infant characteristics associated with non-accidental trauma risk, alongside frequent crying and special needs/disabilities."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ premature prematurity preterm \"low birth weight\") (+ maltreatment abuse neglect) (+ \"special health care needs\" \"chronic illness\" \"difficult to care\" caregiver))","reason":"Search for sources that explicitly explain prematurity as part of special health care needs or difficult caregiving, a mechanism already found in strong evidence."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ premature prematurity preterm \"low birth weight\") (+ maltreatment abuse neglect) (+ \"special health care needs\" \"chronic illness\" \"difficult to care\" caregiver))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_03_1112857541#6_1889600581","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q755","rank":3,"snippet":"with extreme prematurity, makes babies more at risk for certain medical conditions, especially neurological problems such as <a href=\"/Article?contentid=847&language=English\">cerebral palsy</a>. </p><h2>What causes premature birth?</h2><p>There are a number of known reasons why some babies are born premature. Some have to do with the condition of the mother, others with the condition of the fetus. </p><p>Maternal causes, or causes having to do with the general condition of the mother, include:</p><ul><li>high blood pressure </li><li>infection </li><li>substance <cover>abuse </li><li>trauma </li><li>chronic illness </li></ul><p>Premature </cover>birth can also come as a result of complications with either the uterus or the placenta. These include:</p><ul><li>cervical incompetence, or an early opening of the cervix </li><li>malformation of the uterus </li><li>an excess of amniotic fluid, which can cause pressure in the uterus, resulting in early contractions and birth </li><li>malformations or early detachment of the placenta </li></ul><p>Premature birth can also be the result of fetal causes, which include:</p><ul><li>infection </li><li>fetal malform\" , \"start_char\"","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_51_1065794891#8_2188160896","rank":1,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_51_1065794891#7_2188158776","rank":2,"relevance":3}]}}
