{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_47_182835647#0_342687890","relevance":2,"reason":"This infant mental health services page directly links infant characteristics such as low birth weight with threatened parent-infant attachment and states that services reduce abuse and neglect. It supports an attachment-based mechanism related to prematurity but does not explicitly discuss premature birth itself or fully explain why prematurity is an abuse risk factor.","learned":"Low birth weight infants may be part of a high-risk group where infant characteristics threaten parent-infant attachment; attachment support services are intended to reduce abuse and neglect."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ premature prematurity preterm \"low birth weight\") (+ \"parent-infant attachment\" bonding attachment) (+ abuse neglect maltreatment) (+ risk factors))","reason":"Continue pursuing the attachment/bonding mechanism with risk-factor language and prematurity/low-birth-weight terms to find more direct evidence."}}
