{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_1458235944#1_2346220220","relevance":0,"reason":"The result is just a broad medical-condition index/list with terms such as abuse and preterm labor; it contains no discussion of prematurity as a child-abuse risk factor.","learned":"The child-factors/difficult-care query can drift to medical index pages."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ premature preterm prematurity \"low birth weight\") (+ \"child abuse\" \"child maltreatment\") (+ \"increased risk\" \"higher risk\") (+ disability disabilities illness))","reason":"Search for authoritative risk-factor summaries that group prematurity/low birth weight with infant illness or disability as child characteristics increasing abuse/maltreatment risk."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ premature preterm prematurity \"low birth weight\") (+ \"child abuse\" \"child maltreatment\") (+ \"increased risk\" \"higher risk\") (+ disability disabilities illness))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_37_1159109955#6_2540828084","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q761","rank":1,"snippet":"15 percent of cerebral palsy that occurs post-natally, the main cause is infection, usually measles. Other post-natal causes are automobile accidents, falls, and <cover>child abuse. Since in many cases the cause of cerebral palsy is difficult to determine, risk factors are difficult to establish with any measure of statistical certainty. However, there is a risk to children who are born prematurely and are of low birth weight when the mother has had a history of reproductive problems. Women who have had multiple miscarriages are at an increased risk of giving birth to a child with cerebral palsy. Statistically, more whites than African-Americans are affected, as are more males than females. [ back to top] What do the different types of CP mean? There are four different types of cerebral palsy. Spastic cerebral palsy is the most common form, affecting approximately 70 percent of all individuals with cerebral palsy.\" , \"start_char\": 2685.000000 , \"title\": \"A closer look at Cerebral Palsy (TARE)\" , \"url\": \"https://www.dfps.state.tx.us/Adoption_and_Foster_Care/About_Our_Children/Disabilities/</cover>cerebral_palsy.asp\" }"}}
