{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_42_475361992#7_921660068","relevance":0,"reason":"This page is about psychiatric disorder risk factors and lists difficult temperament, abuse/neglect, and low birth weight as separate psychiatric risk factors. It does not address why prematurity increases child-abuse risk.","learned":"Difficult temperament and low birth weight can co-occur in broad mental-health risk-factor lists, but this is not child-abuse evidence."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ preterm premature prematurity) \"child maltreatment\" (+ born birth infants) (+ odds risk study))","reason":"Search for research studies directly examining child maltreatment risk among children born preterm/premature, which may provide strong direct evidence."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ preterm premature prematurity) \"child maltreatment\" (+ born birth infants) (+ odds risk study))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_32_782691323#4_1479326011","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q763","rank":1,"snippet":"\"segment\": \"NOT A BRUE Symptoms explained by specific diagnosis (ie, breath holding spell, seizure)? – NOT A BRUE Meets all BRUE criteria? No other explanation? – THIS IS A BRUE Who are lower risk infants? Infants who meet all of the following criteria: Age > 60 days Gestational age ≥ 32 weeks and post-conceptional age ≥ 45 weeks First BRUE (no history of BRUEs) Duration < 1 minute Event did not require CPR by trained medical professional No concerning history or physical exam findings ( Guideline Table 2) Who are higher <cover>risk infants? Those not meeting all of the above criteria (e.g., age ≤ 2 months, prematurity, etc.) History concerning for child maltreatment</cover>Family history of sudden death in first degree relatives Social and environmental issues House mold problems Previous Child Protective Services or Law Enforcement involvement III. What should I do after I risk-stratify my patient? Management of lower risk infants with BRUE In summary, there is no need to engage in unnecessary tests or treatments.\" , \"start_char\": 1961.000000 , \"title\": \"PEM Pearls: Brief Resolved Unexplained Events (BRUE)\" , \"url\": \"https://www.aliem."}}
